# SPIDER's six tracks (pattern.h NTRK) and its engines (dsp/synth_spider.c): a new project is the kit, mono, poly, fm,
# acid and samples (slice). Away from Steps the top row mutes T1-T6, then pad 7 the throws (held, the conductor), pad 8
# the effects' pages (a tap the delay, again the reverb, again back); FADER BANK: T5, T6, both
# returns, the master. seq.mute's bits: 0-5 the tracks, 6 the conductor, 7 the throws, 8 FX I, 9 FX II
wait 300
expect par1.0 6
expect par2.0 1
expect par3.0 0
expect par4.0 3
expect par5.0 2
expect par6.0 5
expect par2.vmode 1
expect par5.vmode 2
tap HOME
expect page Arrange
expect mute 0
tappad 5
expect mute 32
tappad 5
expect mute 0
# pad 7: tapped, the throws; held, the conductor
tappad 6
expect mute 128
tappad 6
expect mute 0
pad 6 100
wait 600
pad 6 0
wait 40
expect mute 64
pad 6 100
wait 600
pad 6 0
wait 40
expect mute 0
# pad 8: the effects' pages: the delay (FX I), the reverb (FX II), back to the page it was on; no mute
shot tracks_mutes.png
tappad 7
expect mute 0
expect page FX_I
shot tracks_fx1.png
tappad 7
expect page FX_II
shot tracks_fx2.png
tappad 7
expect page Arrange
expect mute 0
# the faders: bank 1 the macros of the track the keys play (cutoff, reso, delay, reverb), picked up (a sweep past the
# value, then set; acid: its own cutoff and reso; the kit: none); bank 2 T1-T4; bank 3 T5, T6, both returns, the master
fader 0 0
fader 0 127
fader 0 90
expect par1.level 100
turn ALGO 1
wait 100
expect trk 2
fader 0 0
fader 0 127
fader 0 90
expect par2.cut 90
fader 1 0
fader 1 127
fader 1 20
expect par2.res 20
fader 2 0
fader 2 127
fader 2 40
expect par2.send1 40
fader 3 0
fader 3 127
fader 3 60
expect par2.send2 60
turn ALGO 3
wait 100
expect trk 5
fader 0 0
fader 0 127
fader 0 33
expect par5.e1 33
fader 1 0
fader 1 127
fader 1 77
expect par5.e2 77
smktap FADERBANK
fader 3 64
fader 3 99
expect par4.level 99
smktap FADERBANK
fader 1 64
fader 1 100
expect par6.level 100
fader 2 64
fader 2 90
expect par9.level 90
expect par10.level 90
smktap FADERBANK
turn ALGO -4
wait 100
expect trk 1
# the Mix page: six strips and the two returns
tap GLO
shot tracks_mix.png
# the keybed plays on Steps (the pads are its cells there): a white key on a synth track sounds
tap HOME
turn ALGO 2
wait 200
wav keys_on_steps.wav
key 7 down 100
wait 300
key 7 up
wait 100
wavstop
# T4, fm: its Engine page (the patch's operators), a note
turn ALGO 1
wait 200
tap EDIT
wait 200
expect page Engine
shot tracks_fm.png
wav fm_note.wav
key 12 down 100
wait 400
key 12 up
wait 300
wavstop
# ARP: tapped, the selected track's arp on and off (TP_PLAYER 1, 0); held and let go, its Players page
tap HOME
turn ALGO 1
wait 200
expect trk 5
expect par5.player 0
tap ARP
wait 100
expect par5.player 1
expect page Arrange
tap ARP
wait 100
expect par5.player 0
press ARP
wait 600
release ARP
wait 100
expect page Players
expect par5.player 0
